## 11. Experiments

Tier 0 carries decision boundaries; a go/no-go without a threshold is not a go/no-go. Sample sizes below assume detecting a correlation of 0.6 against a null of 0.4 at 80% power, α = 0.05, which requires n ≈ 180 for paired comparisons — hence the ~200 figure in T0.1. Comparisons in T2.x are paired by claim wherever the same store is used under two policies.

| # | Claim | Test | Boundary |
|---|---|---|---|
| **T0.1** | Claims are individuable as stable behavioral units | ~200 factual claims from an existing benchmark; estimate Reliability and fan-out via retrieval-conditioned accuracy, sampled ablation, and causal tracing; pairwise rank correlation | ρ ≥ 0.6 all pairs → proceed at that granularity. 0.4–0.6 → **re-run at progressively coarser granularity** (binary-search cluster size upward until ρ clears 0.6) and report the granularity at which it does. < 0.4 at every granularity → **stop** |
| **T0.2** | Schema-change degradation is distinguishable from uniform staleness | Two matched sequences: pure fact-additions vs. items whose later members invalidate earlier organizing structure. Ratio of degradation on schema-adjacent vs. schema-neutral held-out items | ≥ 1.5 → accommodation class is real. ≈ 1.0 → collapse to binary routing, drop Mutual entirely |
| **T0.3** | Friction signatures discriminate conflict from ambiguity | Cross-entropy and attention division under (a) conflicting, (b) ambiguous-but-consistent, (c) clean content | (a) separable from (b) and (c) → usable. (a) ≈ (b) → discard the signal |
| **T0.4** | Baseline persistence | Does a salient event durably shift processing of unrelated inputs on unmodified models? | Establishes the baseline any mechanism must beat |
| **T1.1** | Gradient similarity predicts conflict cheaply | Correlate gradient similarity and exclusion-edge presence against offline gradient-conflict measurement | ρ ≥ 0.5 → adopt as online proxy |
| **T1.2** | Cheap Reliability indicators are unbiased with characterizable variance | Correlate retrieval-conditioned accuracy against sampled ablation; estimate bias and variance rather than only correlation | Unbiased with variance small enough for the §5.1 measurement model → proceed. Systematic bias → §5 needs rework |
| **T1.3** | Independence weighting reduces false promotion | Inject low-diversity corroboration alongside genuine corroboration at matched raw counts | Any significant reduction justifies the mechanism |
| **T1.4** | Lazy materialization detects and localizes pretraining conflict | Claims contradicting model priors vs. claims consistent with them; measure separation in suppressed-vs-active disagreement, then test whether one-at-a-time ablation identifies the responsible claim | Detection separation *and* localization accuracy above chance → §10.8 is addressable, not merely detectable |
| **T2.1** | Governance beats accumulation | Full pipeline vs. Zep/Graphiti, Letta, A-MEM, Mem-α on LOCOMO, LongMemEval, DMR | Must win on multi-session consistency specifically |
| **T2.2** | Demotion corrects drift without thrashing | Concept-drift environment; symmetric vs. asymmetric thresholds | Asymmetric must cut oscillation without cutting correction rate |
| **T2.3** | Decay preserves plasticity without losing rare knowledge | Long-horizon mix of high-frequency and low-frequency-high-stakes knowledge, with and without the rarity floor | Capacity must not saturate; rare-item accuracy must hold. Failure without the floor confirms §5.2 |
| **T2.4** | Coexistence beats forced resolution | Contradictions with disjoint applicability domains | Per-domain accuracy exceeds forced-resolution demotion |
| **T2.5** | Abstraction reduces growth without accuracy loss | Long-horizon run with and without Abstractive routing; edge count, storage, regression performance, re-derivation check pass rate | Sub-linear growth within δ → compression works. Accuracy loss or failing re-derivation checks → §10.9 dominates |
| **T2.6** | Signal decomposition beats a unified score | Six §5 signals vs. one score driving all status decisions; metrics: forgetting rate, false-promotion rate, protected-capacity growth, governance compute | Paired comparison on the same store under both policies |
| **T3.1** | Per-stage null test | Disable each stage; measure whether *routing outcomes* differ | No outcome change → delete the stage |
| **T3.2** | Governance closes the cascade gap | Against RippleEdits and MQuAKE directly, and against manuscript-revision cascade benchmarks separately, since these are distinct threads (§1) | The headline external comparison, and the answer to "couldn't better retrieval get most of this more cheaply?" |

